  "name": "Example: Identifying Lines and Their Notation",
  "problem": "What is the correct way to represent the line shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129501/assets/ea118ccb0db48300f671461a5617d1bb7d1679454e083adab43e4fc2d9bc36f0.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Since the line passes through the points $S$ and $T,$ we can represent this line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{ST}\n$$\n\nWe use the \"$\\longleftrightarrow$\" symbol to denote that the line extends forever in **both** directions.",
